<div class="page">
  <header class="wtitle">
    <h1>Deploy framework</h1>
    <p>Fetches the newest wxl-core release, writes the library and the patcher next to Wow.exe, and
      runs the patcher. This is the same thing the first-run form does, offered on its own so a client
      can be brought up to date without going through it again.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <div class="panel wdeploy">
      <%- render("deploy_state", { t = t }) %>

      <% if t.playing then %>
        <span class="alarm"><%- icon("triangle-alert") %>This is the client your active profile
          launches. Wow.exe will be rewritten, with the original kept beside it as
          <code>Wow.exe.orig</code>.</span>
      <% end %>

      <div class="acts">
        <% --[[ The patcher decides whether it has already run and skips a client it has done, so
                there is one button and not two. Offering "repair" beside "install" would be this
                page holding a second opinion about a question the patcher already answers. ]] %>
        <button class="btn primary" <% if not t.set then %>disabled<% end %>
                hx-post="/workspace/client/deploy" hx-target="#wjob" hx-swap="innerHTML">
          <%= t.set and (t.info.patched and t.info.core.present
                         and "Update the framework" or "Set up this client")
                     or "No client set" %>
        </button>
        <span class="note">Wow.exe is kept as <code>Wow.exe.orig</code> before it is touched.</span>
      </div>

      <% --[[ A bare slot. What lands here is a `.job` itself, and giving the container the class too
              stacks two sets of the same spacing, one of which draws nothing. ]] %>
      <div id="wjob"></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
